    "slug": "what-patients-see-when-they-search-your-practice-name-a-brand-search-audit",
    "keyword": "what patients see when they search your practice name: a brand search audit",
    "category": "Checklist",
    "title": "What Patients See When They Search Your Practice Name: A Brand Search Audit",
    "metaTitle": "Brand Search Audit: What Patients See When They Google You",
    "metaDescription": "A ten-minute audit of what appears when someone Googles your practice name: profile, reviews, listings, ads and AI answers, with fixes. (561) 291-2681.",
    "answer": "Many patients Google a practice by name before they call. Search your name in several ways on a phone, record what appears, and fix what is wrong: the wrong phone number, an old address, a competitor ad, a missing profile or a stray directory page. The fixes are mostly ordinary profile and listing work.",
    "author": "Liam Costello",
    "publishDate": "2026-10-09T09:00:00Z",
    "dateModified": "2026-10-09",
    "readMinutes": 7,
    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "Why branded searches matter"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "A referral, a billboard or a doctor's recommendation often ends with the patient typing your name into Google. That search is the moment of truth. What they see decides whether they call, book online or move on. It is also the easiest search to win, because no one else should outrank you for your own name."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "A brand audit takes about ten minutes and shows problems that months of other marketing will not fix."
      },
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "Run the searches"
      },
      {
        "type": "ol",
        "items": [
          "Search your exact practice name on a phone, then on a computer.",
          "Search the name plus your city, plus the word reviews, and plus phone number.",
          "Search each provider's name with the word doctor or therapist and your city.",
          "Search a question like is practice name accepting new patients.",
          "Ask a few AI assistants about your practice and note what they say."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Search from a private window if you can, so personal history does not shape the results, and note the date. Results vary by location, so also ask a friend in another part of town to check."
      },
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "What to check and how to score it"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Check",
          "Good / Fix if"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Google Business Profile panel",
            "Correct name, phone, hours, address, photos. Anything is wrong, old or missing."
          ],
          [
            "Your website",
            "Ranks first or near first. Missing, or a directory outranks it."
          ],
          [
            "Ads above your result",
            "None, or your own. A competitor is bidding on your name."
          ],
          [
            "Reviews and rating",
            "Rating shows, recent reviews are answered. Unanswered or recent complaints."
          ],
          [
            "Directory listings",
            "Consistent details across top results. Old address, phone or provider names."
          ],
          [
            "Local map pack",
            "Your profile shows. You appear under an old name or twice."
          ],
          [
            "AI answers",
            "Accurate summary. Wrong details or missing practice."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "Common problems and where to fix them"
      },
      {
        "type": "ul",
        "items": [
          "Wrong or old details on the Google panel: fix in the profile, using the steps in our guide to [Google knowledge panels for a medical practice](/guides/google-knowledge-panel-for-a-medical-practice).",
          "A second listing: follow [fixing duplicate Google Business Profile listings](/guides/fix-duplicate-google-business-profile-listings).",
          "Old data on directories and maps: use the [local citation building checklist](/guides/local-citation-building-checklist-for-a-medical-practice) and check Apple Maps and Bing too.",
          "A wrong AI answer: see our guide on fixing [wrong information about your practice in an AI chatbot answer](/guides/fix-wrong-information-about-your-practice-in-an-ai-chatbot-answer).",
          "A competitor ad on your name: you may report trademark use through Google's process, or bid on your own name if it is worth the cost."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "Use Search Console to see the pattern"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Google Search Console shows the queries that led people to your site. Filter for queries that contain your practice name to see branded demand over time. A steady line means your name is known. A drop may mean a closed listing or a change in how people find you. Our guide to [reading Google Search Console for a medical practice website](/guides/how-to-read-google-search-console-for-a-medical-practice-website) explains the reports."
      },
      {
        "type": "h2",
        "text": "Make it a habit"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Repeat the audit quarterly, and any time you move, change a provider or change your phone number. Save screenshots with the date so you can see what changed. Include it in your [monthly Google Business Profile maintenance checklist](/guides/monthly-google-business-profile-maintenance-checklist) so it does not depend on anyone remembering."
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "text": "Do not post fake reviews or ask staff to flood the profile to fix a weak rating. Use steady, compliant requests for real feedback instead."
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "What is a brand search?",
        "a": "It is a search that includes your practice name or a provider's name. These searches usually come from people who already heard of you, so they are the most likely to turn into appointments."
      },
      {
        "q": "Why does a directory outrank my own website for my name?",
        "a": "Directories have strong authority and may be better optimized. Make sure your website title uses your full name and city, your profile links to the site, and your listings point to the same address."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I stop a competitor from advertising on my name?",
        "a": "Competitors may be allowed to bid on your name as a keyword, but Google restricts using a trademark in ad text in some cases. You can submit a complaint through Google's process, or run your own ad on your name."
      },
      {
        "q": "How do I find out what AI assistants say about my practice?",
        "a": "Ask them directly the way a patient would, such as who is a good family doctor in your city, and also ask about your practice by name. Record the answers and fix any wrong details at the source."
      },
      {
        "q": "How often should I run this audit?",
        "a": "Every quarter is a good rhythm, plus after any change in address, phone, provider or practice name."
      }
    ],
